  "returns": "record",
  "version": 7,
  "status": "published",
  "description_nl": "2026-10-07: s.44AB for an individual / HUF filing from My return: (a) business turnover over 1 crore (10 crore when cash receipts are 5% or less), (b) professional receipts over 50 lakh (75 lakh), (d) / (e) the presumptive scheme open but a lower profit declared with income above the basic exemption. Any of them: the accounts are audited by a chartered accountant - My return does not file it (the CA-firm side: Intake, Reconcile, Compute, Tax audit). ponytail: cash payments are not asked - the cash receipts stand for both (the proviso asks both at 5% or less); 44AD(4) (left the scheme within five years) not asked. 2026-10-08: s.44AB(a) / (b) provisos: the higher limit (10 crore business, 75 lakh profession) needs BOTH the cash receipts AND the cash payments at 5% or less of the year's receipts / payments - pay_total / pay_cash (until the payments are typed the receipts' share stands for both, and ask_pay says the payments decide the limit). s.44AD(4): one who declared income under 44AD and then not under it in any of the five years after may not use 44AD for the five years after that; s.44AD(5) with s.44AB(e): such a person with income above the basic exemption keeps books and is audited - why ca_audit_44ad4. ad_closed: 44AD chosen while it is closed.",
